  "observations": [
    "Inherited comparison totals are not direct-path coverage. Audit 115 counted 21855 of 36451 plain raw cases and 2920 of 10540 generated floating calls taking the direct path; benchmark rows are entirely direct.",
    "Timing is descriptive: twenty 125 ms trials after 500 ms warmup, below v3 benchmark discipline. Native includes GC; Wasm timing excludes collection. No formal performance qualification or new LL16 credit.",
    "The direct path does not collect. Pressure cases fall back before writes; movement correctness is covered by the slow path and post-growth refresh controls.",
    "The owner must supply digest-bound scalarBytes and scalarDigest to floatingCapabilities. Omitting them retains the reviewed slow service. This integration ships both the reviewed WAT and matching binary.",
    "Owner admission remains trusted single-Worker identity. Fast sufficient-space assurance validates live state; image enumeration occurs at admission/collection, not on each assurance.",
    "Bignum operations and demanding checked floating modes retain JavaScript fallback and private-memory staging. Eligible scalar operations retain ownership checks, boxing, temporary frames and result delivery."
  ],
  "scope": "Both audit-115 runtime proposals accepted and integrated exactly; LL16-a acceptance remains pending and the ledger is unchanged.",
  "verification": "Both proposals rederived against pre-integration source and matched retained bytes; scalar.wat rebuild equals retained binary; unchanged compiler native R6/R6a reused. Integrated execution checks follow.",
